{"name":"Grey Pebble","hex":"#cfcac1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"},{"term":"pebble","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small stone, especially one rounded by the action of water.","A particle from 4 to 64 mm in diameter, following the Wentworth scale."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pave with pebbles.","To deposit water droplets on the ice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pebble"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pebble","blocks":[{"text":"A pebble is a clast of rock with a particle size of 4–64 mm (0.16–2.52 in) based on the Udden-Wentworth scale of sedimentology. Pebbles are generally considered larger than granules and smaller than cobbles. Pebble tools are among the earliest known man-made artifacts, dating from the Palaeolithic period of human history."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Pebble_Dash_%2815366562092%29.jpg/330px-Pebble_Dash_%2815366562092%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pebble","wikidata":"Q14673"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Beac